/**
 * Credentials to connect to a conda repository. By default we do not use any username or password.
 * This will set the credentials for all conda repositories.
 * ```js
 * CondaRepositoryCredentials.setConfigValue("username", "user", ConfigOverride.ENV);
 * CondaRepositoryCredentials.setSecretValue("password", "password", ConfigOverride.ENV);
 * ```
 * If you want to set the credentials for a specific conda repository (i.e. "conda-forge"), you can use the following which will override the previous settings.
 * id of the config is the name of the conda repository.
 * ```js
 * CondaRepositoryCredentials.forId("conda-forge").setConfigValue("username", "conda-forge-user", ConfigOverride.ENV);
 * CondaRepositoryCredentials.forId("conda-forge").setSecretValue("password", "conda-forge-password", ConfigOverride.ENV);
 * ```
 * In the above examples, we use the override level ENV but you can choose any override level you want {@link ConfigOverride}.
 */
type CondaRepositoryCredentials mixes Config, Identified, BasicCredentials, DefaultInstance
